\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Output-distribution alignment is the primary design dimension for perplexity and commonsense reasoning at moderate sparsity (30\%; signal type accounts for the majority of the PPL gap; upper bound); cross-layer coupling contributes task-dependently---substantially for commonsense, marginally for reasoning (3-seed $K{=}4$-corrected; Appendices~\ref{app:k4_downstream},~\ref{app:constraint}; validated at 30\%; at 50\%, allocation confounds prevent reliable attribution).
A $<$1\% predictor reduces TEAL's PPL by 14.5\% via masks 46--68\% divergent from magnitude, with commonsense gains but knowledge regression across scales.
Limitations: MMLU/GSM8K decline, no wall-clock speedup, 7--14B scale.
Code and trained predictors will be released upon acceptance.

